WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:08.720
Avishai, we're meeting here in Jerusalem. Given the topic of our conference 'What Will Save the World?'..

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.160
Jerusalem is a quite curious place.

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:15.090
In Jerusalem there is this claim that they
know what will save the world

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:21.570
the messiah, the new messiah, the return 
of the messiah, Judaism, Christianity, Islam.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:28.480
What's your take on that?

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.320
There is something which is called 
'the Jerusalem syndrome'.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:36.480
The Jerusalem syndrome is that there is 
a certain kind of madness

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.840
which is associated with Jerusalem.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.480
Really mad people coming with visionary ideas about..

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:49.200
.. a sort of global, eschatological ideas.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:57.520
They've really gone raving mad in towns. 
It's a name by now, I think..

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:03.880
..of a genuine..

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.240
..disease.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:16.120
So you basically ask me to talk like someone with 
the Jerusalem syndrome.

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:20.820
First of all, I don't think the world is in danger. I don't think that the world...

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:25.380
I think that basically the world is safer now than..

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:28.520
..than it was fifty years ago.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.560
Then there was the polarity of..

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:36.720
..when people were terrified of nuclear war.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:40.480
The talk about terrorism is overblown.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.200
Not that there is no terrorism.

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:48.700
Unless you call terrorism every organization 
that you dislike.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:51.680
But if by 'terrorism' you mean sort of..

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.760
..yeah there will be more terror.

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:59.360
.. but it's not a danger to the world..

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:01.380
I don't believe that..

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:03.640
..terrorism can stop..

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:09.280
..let's say what the pirates did in the Mediterranean

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:15.640
..they stopped the Mediterranean traffic 
for 400 years, 500 years.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:18.440
I don't think that anything of that sort..

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:20.980
..is about to happen.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:25.460
I'm neither a cultural pessimist, and not an optimist.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.040
I don't see..

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.760
It will be a different world.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:34.660
That people like me will find congenial,
and may be not.

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:36.600
But at least strange.

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:40.080
I'm not adaptable..

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:44.160
..or ready for the gadgets that are now.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.360
The main thing is whether..

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:54.620
.. the Gutenberg revolution:
the printing culture..

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:59.220
..is about to disappear and be replaced
by something else.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:05.120
In some sense it's already happening, on the other hand people are reading more books now than ever.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:09.340
Then ofcourse there's the issue of 
the climate change.

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:16.640
Which I believe is real. So if 'saving the world'
is saving the planet..

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:21.440
..in the sense of doing something 
about the climate change..

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:24.440
..that's a serious problem.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:36.440
I don't believe it can be done on a retail basis, 
that each individual will try to behave.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:39.000
..it's really for the big powers to negotiate.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.920
Namely the United States, China mainly..

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:47.920
.. India, all the places that are developing. That's serious.

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:56.320
But that's about it..

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.040
..what I see as real danger.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:07.360
Our civilization, or these civilizations will be transmuted or will be transformed.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:15.560
Some of us will like the direction in which it is going, some of us not.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:24.280
I hear more and more pessimism around me. I know I'm surrounded by people like me, that are simply aging.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:27.760
And it's a syndrome about us, not about the world.

